{"name":"Mallow Root","hex":"#f8ebde","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mallow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of flowering plants in several genera of the taxonomic family Malvaceae, especially of the genus Malva. Several species are edible by humans.","Larentia clavaria, an uncommon moth found across Eurasia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mallow"},{"term":"root","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of a plant, generally underground, that anchors and supports the plant body, absorbs and stores water and nutrients, and in some plants is able to perform vegetative reproduction.","A root vegetable."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow roots; to enter the earth, as roots; to take root and begin to grow.","To prepare, oversee, or otherwise cause the rooting of cuttings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/root"}],"entries":[{"title":"Root","blocks":[{"text":"In vascular plants, the roots are the organs of a plant that are modified to provide anchorage for the plant and take in water and nutrients into the plant body, which allows plants to grow taller and faster. They are most often below the surface of the soil, but roots can also be aerial or aerating, that is, growing up above the ground or especially above water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Primary_and_secondary_cotton_roots.jpg/330px-Primary_and_secondary_cotton_roots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root","wikidata":"Q41500"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/CSIRO_ScienceImage_11626_Barley_root.jpg/500px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_11626_Barley_root.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/CSIRO_ScienceImage_11626_Barley_root.jpg/1280px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_1162